			"32": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: SUBTRACTING TEXTURES\n\nIn this example we are subtracting the circle shape from the test card, leaving a hole in the middle.\nNote that subtracting textures is done on a per pixel basis and that a pixel is essentially a float 4 (r,g,b,a).\nSo here we are subtracting white(1,1,1,1) from the testcard, creating the hole.\nBut using another color than pure white will only result in a partial subtraction.\nSubtracting red (1,0,0,1) will remove all the red from the pixels."
					}
				},
